#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Installation ISOs for Windows VMs and Maintenance Windows (tools/WINISO.md).

  locachy-winiso path windows|virtio-win [--lang L]
  locachy-winiso fetch windows [--lang L]
  locachy-winiso check [--lang L]

path prints one absolute path and exits 0, or exits 3 when that ISO is not
available. virtio-win is the ISO of the virtio-win package; windows is the
Windows 11 ISO the last successful fetch verified (with --lang: that language).

fetch downloads the Windows installation ISO from Microsoft into
/var/lib/locachy/isos with one chain of requests: the download page (its table
of SHA-256 values), Microsoft's download service (the link), the ISO; curl
continues a partial file a stopped fetch left. The file is kept only when its
SHA-256 equals the value Microsoft publishes for that language. The language is
--lang, else rc.conf's language, else en-US. A refusal or any answer from
Microsoft that is not a success ends the fetch at once: nothing is tried again
and no other source is used; the person gives a path instead. Online, fetch is
the system job winiso-fetch.

check runs the same language resolution and single-shot Microsoft chain (page,
session registration, language list, x64 link) and verifies the download server
accepts one Range: bytes=0-0 request, without downloading the ISO, touching
/var/lib/locachy/isos, or enqueuing a system job.

Exit status: 0 done, 1 failed here, 2 wrong use, 3 not available (path),
4 Microsoft refused or did not answer with success (for fetch: give a path,
and a partial download is kept for a later fetch), 5 the SHA-256 did not match
(the download is deleted).
"""
